module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.QuasicoherentSectionsColimit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.SectionsColimitLargeIndexCounterexample

/-!
# Stacks 07SI for a limit situation with uniformly bounded base changes

Stacks 07SI reads:

> Notation and assumptions as in Situation 084R. Suppose that `ℱ₀` is a quasi-coherent sheaf
> on `X₀`. Set `ℱᵢ = f_{0i}^*ℱ₀` for `i ≥ 0` and set `ℱ = f_0^*ℱ₀`. Then
> `Γ(X, ℱ) = colim_{i ≥ 0} Γ(Xᵢ, ℱᵢ)`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.isSectionsColimit` proves it on the bounded big fppf site
of this library for an index set of cardinality below the cofinality of the site's size cutoff.
This file proves it under a different size condition: an index set of cardinality below the
cutoff itself, together with a uniform bound below the cutoff on the base changes of the stages
along objects of the site (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.BaseChangeSizeBounded`). Neither condition
implies the other in general, and the second covers systems the first excludes, such as a
Noetherian approximation of an affine scheme `Spec ℤ[x_α : α < λ]` with `λ` below the cutoff but
above its cofinality.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.exists_relationCover_stages_limitBridges`: an affine
  étale cover of the relation of an affine chart, valid at every stage and, for **every** pair of
  limit bridges of the two chart systems, at the limit.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.isSectionsColimit_of_isQuasicoherent_of_limitBridge`:
  the assertion of Stacks 07SI for a quasi-coherent `ℱ₀`, given that the limit is an algebraic
  space and that every affine chart system at the chosen stage has a limit bridge.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.isAlgebraicSpace_of_baseChangeSizeBounded` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.chartLimitBridgeOfBaseChangeSizeBounded`: the limit is
  an algebraic space, and every affine chart system has a limit bridge, under the size condition
  of this file.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.isSectionsColimit_of_baseChangeSizeBounded`:
  **Stacks 07SI** under that size condition.

## Implementation notes

*Why some size condition is needed.* Stacks works on a site fixed large enough for its
constructions (Tag 07SD); on a bounded site this must be said. With no condition the statement
is false (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.Refute07SI.not_forall_isSectionsColimit`): for a field `F` of
cardinality at least the cutoff, the system of the spectra of the subrings of `F` generated by
its finite subsets has as limit in the site the empty algebraic space, whose sections vanish,
while the colimit of the sections at the stages is `F`. The limit
of the charts as schemes is `Spec F`, which is not an object of the site; the size condition is
exactly what puts the limits of the chart systems back into the site.

*The proof.* Every use of the index bound in the proof of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.isSectionsColimit_of_isQuasicoherent` is through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.chartLimitBridge`, the limit bridge of a chart system.
The proof is redone here over an arbitrary family of limit bridges, and the family is then
supplied by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AffineChartSystem.limitBridgeOfBaseChangeSizeBounded`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07SI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07SD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07SF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 084R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/084R)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Cardinal Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}
  {hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u})} {X : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u}
  (A : LimitSituation B S hS hZ X)

/-! ### The cover of the relation, for arbitrary limit bridges -/

/-- **An affine étale cover of the relation of an affine chart, valid at every stage and at the
limit, for any limit bridges.**  This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.exists_relationCover_stages_limit` with the limit clause
stated for an arbitrary limit bridge of each of the two chart systems instead of for the bridges
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.chartLimitBridge` built from an index bound; the pasting
argument at the limit uses only the fields of a limit bridge. -/
theorem exists_relationCover_stages_limitBridges {U₀ : BigAffineFppf B S hS}
    {f₀ : yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj U₀) ⟶ A.system.obj (op A.base)}
    (hf₀ : IsEtaleChart B S hS (A.system.obj (op A.base)) (CostructuredArrow.mk f₀))
    (hsurj : IsSurjective B S hS f₀) :
    ∃ (W₀ : BigAffineFppf B S hS)
      (g₀ : yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj W₀) ⟶ A.system.obj (op A.base))
      (hg₀ : IsEtaleChart B S hS (A.system.obj (op A.base)) (CostructuredArrow.mk g₀))
      (t v : yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj W₀) ⟶
        yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj U₀))
      (ht : t ≫ f₀ = g₀) (hv : v ≫ f₀ = g₀),
      (∀ (i : A.Stages) (N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS (A.stage i.1).obj (A.stage i.1).property)
        (x : (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.stage i.1) N).obj.obj
          (op (A.stagesEtaleChart (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) hf₀ i))),
        (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.stage i.1) N).obj.map
            (A.stagesEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) hf₀ (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) hg₀ ht i).op x =
          (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.stage i.1) N).obj.map
            (A.stagesEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) hf₀ (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) hg₀ hv i).op x →
        ∃ σ : N.sections, σ.val (op (A.stagesEtaleChart (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) hf₀ i)) = x) ∧
      (∀ (hX : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X)
        (LU : AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀))
        (LW : AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀))
        (N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS (A.limitSpace hX).obj (A.limitSpace hX).property)
        (x : (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) N).obj.obj
          (op (A.limitEtaleChart (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU hf₀))),
        (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) N).obj.map
            (A.limitEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) LW
              hf₀ hg₀ ht).op x =
          (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) N).obj.map
            (A.limitEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) LW
              hf₀ hg₀ hv).op x →
        ∃ σ : N.sections, σ.val (op (A.limitEtaleChart (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU hf₀)) = x) := by
  obtain ⟨T, τ, υ, hT, hτe, -⟩ := exists_etale_kernelPair B S hS f₀ hf₀
  have hU₀c : CompactSpace
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj U₀)) := by
    have : IsAffine
        ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj U₀)) :=
      U₀.property
    infer_instance
  have hTc : CompactSpace ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T) :=
    compactSpace_of_isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ (A.quasiSeparated A.base) hT hU₀c hU₀c
  obtain ⟨T₁, c, hT₁, hcs, hce⟩ :=
    (isQuasiCompactSpace_iff_exists_affine_etale_surjective_cover B S hS (yoneda.obj T)
      (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS T)).1 (isQuasiCompactSpace_yoneda B S hS T hTc)
  let W₀ : BigAffineFppf B S hS := ⟨T₁, hT₁⟩
  let c' : yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj W₀) ⟶ yoneda.obj T := c
  have hc' : IsSurjective B S hS c' := isSurjective_of_presheafSurjective B S hS c hcs
  let g₀ := c' ≫ yoneda.map τ ≫ f₀
  have hg₀ : IsEtaleChart B S hS (A.system.obj (op A.base)) (CostructuredArrow.mk g₀) :=
    presheaf_etale_of_isEtale B S hS (isEtale_comp B S hS hce
      (isEtale_of_presheaf_etale B S hS (etale_comp_of_scheme B S hS τ f₀ hτe hf₀)))
  have ht : (c' ≫ yoneda.map τ) ≫ f₀ = g₀ := Category.assoc _ _ _
  have hv : (c' ≫ yoneda.map υ) ≫ f₀ = g₀ :=
    (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans (congrArg (c' ≫ ·) hT.w.symm)
  let C := A.chartSystem U₀ f₀
  let E := A.chartSystem W₀ g₀
  refine ⟨W₀, g₀, hg₀, c' ≫ yoneda.map τ, c' ≫ yoneda.map υ, ht, hv, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro i N x hx
    let j := (stagesOverEquivalence A).functor.obj (op i)
    refine exists_sections_eq_of_relationCover N (A.isSurjective_stagesEtaleChart C hf₀ hsurj i)
      _ _ (fun {R p q} k K hkp hkq => ?_) x hx
    have hk : ∀ {m : R ⟶ A.stagesEtaleChart C hf₀ i} {τ' : _} (hτ' : τ' ≫ f₀ = g₀),
        k ≫ m = A.stagesEtaleChartMap C hf₀ E hg₀ hτ' i →
        yoneda.map ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS (A.stage i.1).1).map k) ≫
          yoneda.map ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS (A.stage i.1).1).map m)
            = C.inducedPresheafMap E hτ' j := fun hτ' hm => by
      rw [← yoneda.map_comp, ← Functor.map_comp, hm]
      exact C.yoneda_map_inducedMap E hτ' j
    obtain ⟨h, hsq⟩ := exists_isPullback_of_relationCover (A.system.map j.hom) (C.isPullback j)
      (E.isPullback j) hT c' ht (C.inducedPresheafMap_comp_stageMap E ht j)
      ((C.inducedPresheafMap_comp_baseMap E ht j).trans (Category.assoc _ _ _))
      ((C.inducedPresheafMap_comp_baseMap E hv j).trans (Category.assoc _ _ _)) K _
      (hk ht hkp) (hk hv hkq)
    exact surjective_pointsMap_of_isPullback B S hS hsq hc'
  · intro hX LC LE N x hx
    refine exists_sections_eq_of_relationCover N (A.isSurjective_limitEtaleChart C LC hf₀ hsurj)
      _ _ (fun {R p q} k K hkp hkq => ?_) x hx
    have hia : ∀ {τ' : yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj W₀) ⟶
        yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj U₀)} (hτ' : τ' ≫ f₀ = g₀),
        yoneda.map (AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge.inducedMap LC LE hτ') ≫ LC.toBase
          = LE.toBase ≫ τ' := fun hτ' => by
      rw [AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge.yoneda_map_inducedMap,
        AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge.inducedPresheafMap_comp_toBase]
    have hk : ∀ {m : R ⟶ A.limitEtaleChart C LC hf₀} {τ' : _} (hτ' : τ' ≫ f₀ = g₀),
        k ≫ m = A.limitEtaleChartMap C LC E LE hf₀ hg₀ hτ' →
        yoneda.map ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS (A.limitSpace hX).1).map k) ≫
          yoneda.map ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS (A.limitSpace hX).1).map m)
            = yoneda.map (AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge.inducedMap LC LE hτ') :=
      fun hτ' hm => by
      rw [← yoneda.map_comp]
      exact congrArg yoneda.map
        (((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS (A.limitSpace hX).1).map_comp k _).symm.trans
          (congrArg (SmallEtale.toOver B S hS (A.limitSpace hX).1).map hm))
    obtain ⟨h, hsq⟩ := exists_isPullback_of_relationCover (A.π.app (op A.base))
      (A.isPullback_limitChartToSpace C LC) (A.isPullback_limitChartToSpace E LE) hT c' ht
      (A.yoneda_map_inducedMap_comp_limitChartToSpace C LC E LE ht)
      ((hia ht).trans (Category.assoc _ _ _)) ((hia hv).trans (Category.assoc _ _ _)) K _
      (hk ht hkp) (hk hv hkq)
    exact surjective_pointsMap_of_isPullback B S hS hsq hc'

/-! ### The equalizer presentation at the limit, for arbitrary limit bridges -/

section Cover

variable {U₀ W₀ : BigAffineFppf B S hS}
  {f₀ : yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj U₀) ⟶ A.system.obj (op A.base)}
  {g₀ : yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj W₀) ⟶ A.system.obj (op A.base)}
  {t v : yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj W₀) ⟶
    yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj U₀)}
  (F₀ : Modules.{u, u} B S hS (A.stage A.base).obj (A.stage A.base).property)
  (hf₀ : IsEtaleChart B S hS (A.system.obj (op A.base)) (CostructuredArrow.mk f₀))
  (hg₀ : IsEtaleChart B S hS (A.system.obj (op A.base)) (CostructuredArrow.mk g₀))
  (ht : t ≫ f₀ = g₀) (hv : v ≫ f₀ = g₀)
  (LU : AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀))
  (LW : AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀))

/-- **The compatibilities `hpi` and `hqi` at the limit, for arbitrary limit bridges**: restriction
from `U` to `W` after the chart section map `ℱᵢ(Uᵢ) → ℱ(U)` is the chart section map
`ℱᵢ(Wᵢ) → ℱ(W)` after restriction from `Uᵢ` to `Wᵢ`. -/
theorem chartLimitCoverRestriction_chartLimitInclusion_of_limitBridge
    (hX : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X) {τ : _} (hτ : τ ≫ f₀ = g₀) (i : A.Stages)
    (y : A.chartStageSections F₀ hf₀ i) :
    (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) (A.limitModule F₀ hX)).obj.map
        (A.limitEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) LW hf₀ hg₀ hτ).op
        (A.chartLimitInclusion (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) hf₀ F₀ LU hX i y)
      = A.chartLimitInclusion (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) hg₀ F₀ LW hX i
          (A.chartStageCoverRestriction F₀ hf₀ hg₀ hτ i y) :=
  chartPullbackSectionMap_naturality (A.projection hX i.1) (A.stageModule F₀ i)
    (A.limitModule F₀ hX) (A.stageProjectionComparison F₀ hX i)
    (A.limitChartDiagram (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) hf₀ LU hX i)
    (A.limitChartDiagram (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) hg₀ LW hX i)
    (A.limitEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) LW hf₀ hg₀ hτ)
    (A.stagesEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) hf₀ (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) hg₀ hτ i)
    (AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge.inducedMap_comp_π LU LW hτ
      ((stagesOverEquivalence A).functor.obj (op i))) y

/-- **The presentation over a cover of the relation at the limit, for arbitrary limit bridges**:
`Γ(X, ℱ) ≃ {x : ℱ(U) // a^*x = b^*x}` for the two maps of limit charts `a, b : W ⟶ U`. -/
noncomputable def limitSectionsEquivCoverEqualizerOfLimitBridge (hX : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X)
    (hsurj : IsSurjective B S hS f₀)
    (hglue : ∀ (N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS (A.limitSpace hX).obj (A.limitSpace hX).property)
      (x : (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) N).obj.obj
        (op (A.limitEtaleChart (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU hf₀))),
      (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) N).obj.map
          (A.limitEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) LW
            hf₀ hg₀ ht).op x =
        (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) N).obj.map
          (A.limitEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) LW
            hf₀ hg₀ hv).op x →
      ∃ σ : N.sections, σ.val (op (A.limitEtaleChart (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU hf₀)) = x) :
    A.limitSections F₀ hX ≃
      {x : (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) (A.limitModule F₀ hX)).obj.obj
          (op (A.limitEtaleChart (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU hf₀)) //
        (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) (A.limitModule F₀ hX)).obj.map
            (A.limitEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) LW
              hf₀ hg₀ ht).op x =
          (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) (A.limitModule F₀ hX)).obj.map
            (A.limitEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) LW
              hf₀ hg₀ hv).op x} :=
  moduleSectionsEquivCoverEqualizer (A.limitModule F₀ hX)
    (A.isSurjective_limitEtaleChart (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU hf₀ hsurj) _ _
    (hglue (A.limitModule F₀ hX))

/-- The presentation over a cover of the relation at the limit is evaluation at the chart. -/
theorem limitSectionsEquivCoverEqualizerOfLimitBridge_apply (hX : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X)
    (hsurj : IsSurjective B S hS f₀)
    (hglue : ∀ (N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS (A.limitSpace hX).obj (A.limitSpace hX).property)
      (x : (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) N).obj.obj
        (op (A.limitEtaleChart (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU hf₀))),
      (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) N).obj.map
          (A.limitEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) LW
            hf₀ hg₀ ht).op x =
        (moduleSetSheaf B S hS (A.limitSpace hX) N).obj.map
          (A.limitEtaleChartMap (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) LW
            hf₀ hg₀ hv).op x →
      ∃ σ : N.sections, σ.val (op (A.limitEtaleChart (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU hf₀)) = x)
    (σ : A.limitSections F₀ hX) :
    (A.limitSectionsEquivCoverEqualizerOfLimitBridge F₀ hf₀ hg₀ ht hv LU LW hX hsurj hglue σ).1
      = moduleSectionValue (A.limitModule F₀ hX) σ
          (op (A.limitEtaleChart (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) LU hf₀)) :=
  moduleSectionsEquivCoverEqualizer_apply _ _ _ _ _ σ

end Cover

/-! ### Stacks 07SI over arbitrary limit bridges -/

variable (F₀ : Modules.{u, u} B S hS (A.stage A.base).obj (A.stage A.base).property)

/-- **The global sections of the inverse image of a quasi-coherent module to the limit are the
filtered colimit of its global sections at the stages, given limit bridges.**  The assertion of
Stacks 07SI holds as soon as the limit is an algebraic space and every affine chart system at the
chosen stage has a limit bridge. This is the proof of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.isSectionsColimit_of_isQuasicoherent` with the bridges
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.chartLimitBridge` replaced by the given family `LB`. -/
theorem isSectionsColimit_of_isQuasicoherent_of_limitBridge (hX : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X)
    (LB : ∀ (V : BigAffineFppf B S hS)
      (g : yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj V) ⟶ A.system.obj (op A.base)),
      AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge (A.chartSystem V g))
    (hF₀ : F₀.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) :
    A.IsSectionsColimit F₀ hX := by
  obtain ⟨U₀, f₀, hf₀, hsurj⟩ :=
    LimitSituation.exists_affine_isSurjective_etaleChart_stage B S hS A A.base
  obtain ⟨W₀, g₀, hg₀, t, v, ht, hv, hglue, hglueL⟩ :=
    A.exists_relationCover_stages_limitBridges hf₀ hsurj
  have hglueX := hglueL hX (LB U₀ f₀) (LB W₀ g₀)
  exact A.isSectionsColimit_of_equalizerPresentation F₀ hX
    (fun _ _ h y => A.chartStageCoverRestriction_chartStageTransition F₀ hf₀ hg₀ ht h y)
    (fun _ _ h y => A.chartStageCoverRestriction_chartStageTransition F₀ hf₀ hg₀ hv h y)
    (fun i y => A.chartLimitCoverRestriction_chartLimitInclusion_of_limitBridge F₀ hf₀ hg₀
      (LB U₀ f₀) (LB W₀ g₀) hX ht i y)
    (fun i y => A.chartLimitCoverRestriction_chartLimitInclusion_of_limitBridge F₀ hf₀ hg₀
      (LB U₀ f₀) (LB W₀ g₀) hX hv i y)
    (A.stageSectionsEquivCoverEqualizer F₀ hf₀ hg₀ ht hv hsurj hglue)
    (A.limitSectionsEquivCoverEqualizerOfLimitBridge F₀ hf₀ hg₀ ht hv (LB U₀ f₀) (LB W₀ g₀) hX
      hsurj hglueX)
    (fun i j h σ =>
      ((A.stageSectionsEquivCoverEqualizer_apply F₀ hf₀ hg₀ ht hv hsurj hglue j
            (A.stageTransition F₀ i j h σ)).trans
          (A.moduleSectionValue_stageTransition (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) hf₀ F₀ h σ)).trans
        (congrArg (A.chartStageTransition (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) hf₀ F₀ h)
          (A.stageSectionsEquivCoverEqualizer_apply F₀ hf₀ hg₀ ht hv hsurj hglue i σ).symm))
    (fun i σ =>
      ((A.limitSectionsEquivCoverEqualizerOfLimitBridge_apply F₀ hf₀ hg₀ ht hv (LB U₀ f₀)
            (LB W₀ g₀) hX hsurj hglueX (A.stageProjection F₀ hX i σ)).trans
          (A.moduleSectionValue_stageProjection (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) hf₀ F₀
            (LB U₀ f₀) hX i σ)).trans
        (congrArg (A.chartLimitInclusion (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) hf₀ F₀ (LB U₀ f₀) hX i)
          (A.stageSectionsEquivCoverEqualizer_apply F₀ hf₀ hg₀ ht hv hsurj hglue i σ).symm))
    (A.isStagesColimit_chartSections_of_isQuasicoherent (A.chartSystem U₀ f₀) hf₀ F₀ hF₀
      (LB U₀ f₀) hX)
    (A.isStagesColimit_chartSections_of_isQuasicoherent (A.chartSystem W₀ g₀) hg₀ F₀ hF₀
      (LB W₀ g₀) hX)

/-! ### The size condition -/

/-- **The limit of a limit situation is an algebraic space**, for an index set below the site's
size cutoff whose stages have uniformly bounded base changes. This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAlgebraicSpace_limit_of_baseChangeSizeBounded` transported to the
presheaf the situation is attached to along the limiting cone it carries; the bound on the hom
types is automatic, the morphisms of a preorder being subsingletons. -/
theorem isAlgebraicSpace_of_baseChangeSizeBounded (hI : #A.I < B.cutoff)
    (hB : BaseChangeSizeBounded B S hS A.system) : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X := by
  have := A.hasLimit
  have hSize' : #A.Iᵒᵖ < B.cutoff := A.mk_op ▸ hI
  exact isAlgebraicSpace_of_iso B S hS (limit.isoLimitCone ⟨A.cone, A.isLimitCone⟩)
    (isAlgebraicSpace_limit_of_baseChangeSizeBounded B S hS A.system hSize' B.aleph0_lt_cutoff
      (fun i j => (A.mk_hom_lt_aleph0 i j).le) (fun i => A.isAlgebraicSpace i.unop)
      (fun {_ _} f => A.transition_affine f) hB)

/-- **The limit of an affine chart system of a limit situation**, as a limit bridge, for an index
set below the site's size cutoff whose stages have uniformly bounded base changes. This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AffineChartSystem.limitBridgeOfBaseChangeSizeBounded`. -/
noncomputable def chartLimitBridgeOfBaseChangeSizeBounded (hI : #A.I < B.cutoff)
    (hB : BaseChangeSizeBounded B S hS A.system) (V : BigAffineFppf B S hS)
    (g : yoneda.obj ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj V) ⟶ A.system.obj (op A.base)) :
    AffineChartSystem.LimitBridge (A.chartSystem V g) :=
  (A.chartSystem V g).limitBridgeOfBaseChangeSizeBounded (A.mk_op ▸ hI) B.aleph0_lt_cutoff
    (fun i j => (A.mk_hom_lt_aleph0 i j).le) hB

/-- **Stacks 07SI.**  In Situation 084R, let `ℱ₀` be a quasi-coherent module on `X₀`, and set
`ℱᵢ = f_{0i}^*ℱ₀` and `ℱ = f_0^*ℱ₀`.  Then `Γ(X, ℱ) = colim_{i ≥ 0} Γ(Xᵢ, ℱᵢ)`, in the
elementwise form `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation.IsSectionsColimit`.

The size condition, an index set below the cutoff with uniformly bounded base changes, is how the
bounded site reads the size conventions of the source (Tag 07SD); with no size condition the
statement is false, by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.Refute07SI.not_forall_isSectionsColimit`. -/
@[stacks 07SI "Situation 084R on the bounded site, with the size conventions of Tag 07SD read as an index set below the cutoff with uniformly bounded base changes of the stages; with no size condition the statement is false, Refute07SI.not_forall_isSectionsColimit"]
theorem isSectionsColimit_of_baseChangeSizeBounded (hI : #A.I < B.cutoff)
    (hB : BaseChangeSizeBounded B S hS A.system) (hF₀ : F₀.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) :
    A.IsSectionsColimit F₀ (A.isAlgebraicSpace_of_baseChangeSizeBounded hI hB) :=
  A.isSectionsColimit_of_isQuasicoherent_of_limitBridge F₀ _
    (A.chartLimitBridgeOfBaseChangeSizeBounded hI hB) hF₀

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space.LimitSituation

